		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "effect",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 29,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Bulging Lines - ribbons fly out of the depth of the picture towards the viewer, over the floor in front of the projection. Driven by the Motion Bridge field (Spout): the ribbons flow around what stands on the floor and flutter strongly where something moves, then calm down. Near the projection = near in the picture (bottom), far = towards the horizon. Calm without the bridge; transparent background. Needs the Motion Bridge tool. In Arena, load the Spout source 'Motion Bridge' as a clip at its own size, set the layer's Auto Size to Stretch, put this patch on the clip (after its Transform) and set the layer's blend mode to Alpha. Scale sizes everything relative to the output height; Clock (0 to 1000) drives the flight: set its phase source to Timeline, Duration 1000 s; the flutter runs in real time. Ribbons: Ribbon Density (ribbons per output height), Ribbon Width, Ribbon Color, Ribbons Opacity. View: Horizon Y (height of the horizon above the bottom edge, in output heights). Physics: Avoid Strength (how far the ribbons move around what stands there), Flutter Strength, Flutter Life (seconds until the flutter has calmed down). Show Field shows the field on the floor for setting up. Shader: Resource/BulgingLines.fs.",
			"displayName": "Bulging Lines",
			"identifier": "18231369-8d7a-4444-b13d-7ec2fa10beec",
			"licenseName": "Unlicense",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
